the update-rc.d class.

193
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:28,668
And this is going to
bring in a capability for

194
00:13:28,668 --> 00:13:32,096
installing INITSCRIPT for you.

195
00:13:32,096 --> 00:13:36,892
And this is again the class that's going
to handle everything that we need to do in

196
00:13:36,892 --> 00:13:39,158
in order to install our INITSCRIPTS.

197
00:13:39,158 --> 00:13:45,173
And then you need to define INITSCRIPT
packages equals your package name.

198
00:13:45,173 --> 00:13:50,345
And this just flags your package
as one which uses INISCRIPTS for

199
00:13:50,345 --> 00:13:51,887
the build system.

200
00:13:51,887 --> 00:13:57,364
And then finally, you'd say,
INITSCRIPT_NAME:${PN} and

201
00:13:57,364 --> 00:14:01,188
set that value to your start-script-name.

202
00:14:01,188 --> 00:14:06,725
So similar to what we did with buildroot,
we will define a start-script that does

203
00:14:06,725 --> 00:14:12,355
the start-stop commands and just reference
that here within INITSCRIPT_NAME.

204
00:14:12,355 --> 00:14:14,902
And then similarly in the do install,

205
00:14:14,902 --> 00:14:19,606
you're going to have to install
the start-script init.d directory.

206
00:14:19,606 --> 00:14:25,696
And note here, we do an install -d of
the SC init.d directory just to make sure

207
00:14:25,696 --> 00:14:31,718
we've got that set up in our target root
of S before we try to install the file.

208
00:14:31,718 --> 00:14:35,558
Your start-script, to that location.

209
00:14:35,558 --> 00:14:40,140
And I included a link here
about the update-rc.d class.

210
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:44,367
And I wanted to note that some of
the documentation online still

211
00:14:44,367 --> 00:14:47,407
